# Never commit the real environment / secrets — only .env.example is tracked.
.env
agent.env
config/

# NARROW EXCEPTION to `config/` above. The recyclarr config is declarative and
# secret-free: API keys are `!env_var` placeholders resolved at run time from an
# untracked recyclarr.env (0600) on grey. Version-controlling it is the whole
# point — otherwise a recyclarr run silently reverts the quality policy.
#
# The whitelist is per-file ON PURPOSE. `config/` on the box also holds
# config.xml files carrying live API keys and qbit-manage's password, so a
# directory-wide negation would be a credential leak waiting to happen. Anything
# not named below stays ignored. Do NOT broaden this to `!config/**`.
!config/
config/*
!config/README.md
!config/recyclarr/
config/recyclarr/*
!config/recyclarr/recyclarr.yml
!config/recyclarr/generate.py
!config/recyclarr/sync-to-grey.sh

# Python build artifacts from the intake bot.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
